        "role": "user",
        "content": "A newly deployed workload in namespace scenario-test is failing to start. Investigate and tell me the exact reason."
      }
    ],
    "final_text": "INVESTIGATION_PLAN:\n- Inspect the pod `bad-image-app-76d9cff595-8tq4p` in the `scenario-test` namespace for detailed failure information using `kubectl describe pod`.\n- Review the warning events in the `scenario-test` namespace to confirm the error sequence.\n- Verify the image reference and pull-secret presence for the failing pod.\n\nExecuting the necessary tool calls in parallel.The newly deployed workload in the `scenario-test` namespace is failing due to an `ImagePullBackOff` error. The exact reason is:\n\n- The pod `bad-image-app-76d9cff595-8tq4p` is attempting to pull the image `nginx:99.99.99-does-not-exist`, which does not exist in the Docker registry. The error message confirms that the image tag `99.99.99-does-not-exist` is invalid and cannot be resolved.\n\n### Suggested Fix:\nUpdate the deployment to use a valid image tag for `nginx`. For example, you can use the latest stable version `nginx:latest` or another known valid tag.\n\nWould you like me to apply this fix?",
